<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Rooke</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1650–1709</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Also known as Sir George Rooke</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sir George Rooke was an English admiral. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/war-of-the-spanish-succession">War of the Spanish Succession</a> he destroyed the Spanish treasure fleet and its French escort at Vigo Bay in 1702. In August 1704 his Anglo-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> fleet captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gibraltar">Gibraltar</a> in the name of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> claimant Charles, and days later he fought the French fleet at the Battle of Málaga.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-rooke.jpg" alt="George Rooke" width="320" height="394" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Michael Dahl · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_Rooke.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
